{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And the sense of 'הנני מפרך'.</b> According to the Gaon [Saadia], who said that 'HaShem said to me, I will make you fruitful' — yet no son was born to me; only Rachel died; and now I know that on account of sons born to you He said 'I will make you fruitful' — this interpretation has no sense or savor, for what difference is there between the sons of Joseph and the sons of Reuben? And furthermore, Benjamin was born to him after this prophecy. And the correct interpretation in my eyes is that he said: 'HaShem said to me that the land of Canaan shall be an everlasting possession for my seed, and I give you the birthright in the inheritance of the land.' And Ephraim and Manasseh shall take their portion in the land, just as Reuben and Simeon — who are the eldest of my sons — shall take. And whoever you beget after Ephraim and Manasseh shall be called by the name of their aforementioned brothers, who inherit with them in their inheritance. And the commentator who said that 'ומולדתך' refers to the sons of Machir, who will be born upon Joseph's knees — his words are not right in my eyes, for what sense is there in 'by the name of their brothers'? And if one argues that we find no other sons for Joseph, this too is no argument, for it is possible that there were, and because they inherited with their brothers Scripture did not mention them — and there are many such cases."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:17.099746415Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}